  "releaseNotes": "v8.6.0\n\n\t\t\tmogwai.assert — new assertion primitive. Accepts a boolean or a list (auto-evaluated). Raises MW.9 on failure with a display-only message; error.last returns MW.9. Raises MW.24 if a list pushes more than one value, MW.21 if the result is not boolean.\n\n\t\t\tObject-Oriented Programming : MOGWAI now supports a complete class system\n\t\t\t- class 'Name' do { ... }` defines a class with private: and public: sections.\n\t\t\t- Properties declared with a type sigil (e.g. .number, .string), initialized to empty.\n\t\t\t- Methods declared as named code blocks within a section.\n\t\t\t- Optional lifecycle hooks: onInit: (called on new) and onFree: (called on free).\n\t\t\t- new, creates an instance; each instance receives a unique internal handle (§N).\n\t\t\t- free, destroys an instance and invalidates all references to it.\n\t\t\t- self, automatically injected reference to the current instance inside any method.\n\t\t\t- className:, read-only public property available on every instance; returns the class name as a string.\n\n\t\t\t- MW.95, new error code raised when the reserved property className: is written to or declared in a class definition.\n\n\t\t\tFull changelog: https://github.com/Sydney680928/mogwai/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
